# Python bytecode from running the scripts in scripts/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The payload -- NOT in git, on purpose.
#
# entry/libs/arm64-v8a/ holds the JDK (255 MB), the game jar (83 MB) and the Arc
# natives. Two reasons it stays out:
#
#   1. GitHub rejects any single file over 100 MB on a normal repository, and
#      jdk21/lib/jimg.so is 134 MB. Making it fit would mean Git LFS, which
#      spends most of a free account's 1 GB monthly bandwidth on a single clone.
#   2. It is derivable. Everything in there is produced by the prep_*.py scripts
#      from the inputs listed in README.md, so keeping it in git would be
#      keeping a build artifact.
#
# Prebuilt HAPs (which do contain the payload) are published as Release assets
# instead -- those do not count toward repository size.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
entry/libs/

# tools 形态构建时 `entry/libs/arm64-v8a/` 暂存处（见 scripts/make_store_app.sh）。
# ⛔ 它**必须在 entry/libs/ 之外**：hvigor 会递归收集那里的 `.so`，
#    放进去会让 stash 被打进包。
/.tools-stash/

# make_store_app.sh 的临时文件落点：module.json5 的备份、构建日志。
# 用【仓库内的相对路径】是为了让 bash 与 Windows 版 Python 指向同一处 ——
# 两者对 `/tmp` 的解析不同，用 TEMP 会各写各的（见该脚本里的说明）。
/.store-scratch/

# The INPUTS those scripts assemble entry/libs/ from: the upstream and patched
# game jars, the LWJGL jars and natives, and two files out of the trimmed JDK.
# Same reasoning as entry/libs/ -- large, mostly reproducible, and the parts that
# are not reproducible travel in the payload release instead. The README stays,
# because it is what says which files belong here and which hashes they must have.
payload-src/*
!payload-src/README.md

# Scratch from our own diagnostic runs
*.jpeg
_probe*/
_hapcheck/
_anchorpad/
_build.bat
sy_act*.py
clean_perms.py

# The abandoned C++ shim replacement, kept locally but not published.
#
# libjvm.so declares __cxa_thread_atexit, which neither the JDK's shim nor OHOS
# libc was believed to export, so a replacement shim was built to supply it. It
# worked; what retired it was finding a working configuration that does not need
# it -- the same libjvm.so with the JDK's unmodified shim. Nothing in the build
# references these any more, and CMakeLists.txt explains the reasoning.
#
# Untracked rather than deleted: they are the readable record of a real
# measurement. See entry/src/main/cpp/CMakeLists.txt.
/scripts/make_cxxabi_real.py
/entry/src/main/cpp/cxatls.c
/entry/src/main/cpp/libcxxabi_real.so

# Signing config with real key paths/passwords. Never commit these: they are
# machine-specific, and the password blobs do not belong in a public repository.
#
# TWO files hold signing material, and until 2026-09-24 only the first was listed
# here -- while the second was the one that actually carried it:
#
#   build-profile.local.json5   DevEco's own local override. Listed here from the
#                               start, and it holds a signing config.
#   /build-profile.json5        THE ROOT ONE. DevEco Studio writes the signing
#                               config straight into it -- certpath, keyAlias,
#                               keyPassword, profile, storeFile, storePassword.
#
# The root file used to be kept out of the way with `git update-index
# --skip-worktree`, which does work -- but that flag lives in THIS MACHINE's git
# config and is not carried by the repository. A fresh clone, or a stray
# `--no-skip-worktree`, left it fully exposed, and .gitignore cannot help once a
# file is tracked. The guard now lives here, where it travels with the repo.
#
# The committed skeleton is build-profile.json5.template -- copy it into place:
#     cp build-profile.json5.template build-profile.json5
# entry/build-profile.json5 is a DIFFERENT file (buildOption / targets only, no
# signing material) and stays committed. The leading slash matters: a bare
# `build-profile.json5` would match that one too.
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT `*.json5`. That glob gets proposed every so often, and it is
# the wrong axis: .json5 is a FORMAT, not a risk class. What matters is whether a
# file holds secrets, and exactly two do -- both listed by path above.
#
# Eleven other .json5 files here are load-bearing and MUST stay committed:
#     AppScope/app.json5                      versionName / versionCode / bundleName
#     entry/src/main/module.json5             permissions, deviceTypes
#     entry/build-profile.json5               artifactName
#     entry/src/main/cpp/types/*/oh-package.json5   one per NAPI module
#     oh-package.json5, *-lock.json5, code-linter.json5, hvigor-config.json5
# A glob would not touch the already-tracked ones anyway (.gitignore has no effect
# on tracked files), so it would add ZERO protection while silently hiding every
# FUTURE .json5 from `git status` -- a new NAPI module's oh-package.json5 would
# never get committed and a fresh clone would not build, with nothing on screen
# to say why. Silent, and exactly the class of failure this section exists to
# prevent.
/build-profile.json5

# DevEco's own local override. It also holds a signing config, and it was the
# only one of the two listed here before 2026-09-24.
build-profile.local.json5

# Diagnostic / measurement harnesses used while developing. They are specific to
# this machine's device ids and paths, and they are not needed to build or run --
# so they stay local. The reasoning they were used for is preserved in the source
# comments, which is where it is useful to anyone else.
esc_ab.sh
quit_timing.sh
jvmrun.sh
tryopts.sh

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Signing material -- NEVER in git.
#
# A .p12 holds the PRIVATE KEY. Anyone who gets it can sign releases as this
# developer, and unlike a leaked password it cannot be rotated without the app
# getting a new certificate. The .cer and .p7b are the public halves and are far
# less dangerous, but they identify the account, so they stay out too.
#
# These patterns are a backstop, not the plan: the real protection is keeping the
# files outside the repository (DevEco defaults to ~/.ohos/config, which is
# already outside). This exists so that dropping one in here "for a moment" does
# not end up committed by a `git add -A`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.p12
*.csr
*.cer
*.p7b

# Release artifacts assembled locally (the payload zip is ~140 MB -- it goes on
# the Releases page, never in git; see the note on entry/libs above).
dist/

# Scratch from crash investigations: pulled faultlogs, sandbox logs, sandbox
# backups, kept packages, extracted sections. All of it is derived from a device
# or a build and none of it belongs in the repository -- and a `git add -A` after
# an investigation should not be able to sweep it in.
_faultlog_*/
_fl[0-9]/
_keep/
_sects/
_sandbox_backup_*/
_crash_*.log
# stderr.log/stdout.log pulled from a device. These are evidence for the rule
# that "probe = 42 means the JVM was created, -1 means create() never returned",
# so they are kept on disk on purpose -- but they are a device's output, not
# source, and two local copies of the same run are not worth a commit.
_stderr_*.log

# tools/probe-mod/build.sh output -- regenerated, and it is copied into
# entry/libs/ (also ignored) where the bundle picks it up.
tools/probe-mod/out/

# scripts/asan.py 存两份被改文件的原状，供 `off` 逐字节还原。
# 它是**临时物料**（由 `on` 生成、`off` 删除），不是源码，⛔ 不该进仓库。
.asan-backup/
